{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost","id":1480206,"title":"What changes have been made to Changeling The Lost?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-05T14:05:54-07:00","id":1480206,"title":"What changes have been made to Changeling The Lost?","content":"I'm a big fan of the series and I have been recently getting back into the game and like to know if there has been any changes to the Seasonal Courts, Entitlements, Contracts and quirks that high wyrd Changelings obtain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T15:20:06-07:00","id":1480214,"title":"","content":"I'm going to assume you mean from 1e to 2e?<br /> <br /> The Seasonal Courts didn't change much practically. There is a new mechanic for when a Court in ascendant that controls the Gentry to help make the Court's protective nature more clear. While they don't stop the Fae completely, they do force and conflicts into specific and predictable patterns that help give the Lost an edge. The metaphysical underpinnings of the Courts is more defined, allowing (in theory, but we don't have Court Contract creation rules) easier construction of alternative Court systems or coexisting Court systems.<br /> <br /> Entitlements have been reworked rather thoroughly. Their mechanics are better defined in general, but the big change is that they're usually more personal now. Entitlements are now unique titles only one being can have at a time. There can be Legion Entitlements, where the stories of multiple Entitlements are closely interconnected allowing for things closer to 1e's organized groups, but while they share an overarching theme, each member has a unique place. There could be The Knights of the Round Table with multiple members, but there can only be one King, one Lancelot, etc.<br /> <br /> Contracts were changed significantly as well. Arcadian Contracts (replacing Universal and Seeming ones) are sorted into six Regalia themes (each Seeming favors one), and withing each Regalia there are common and royal Contracts. Royal are treated as better, mildly, and are more big and flashy than practical and subtle. There are no longer 1-5 ratings in them, each one is a separate power of its own. Arcadian Contracts also have additional bonuses that you get for free if they match your Seeming, but can be learned at cost by anyone. For example Cloak of Night gives a stealth boost to you and Dexterity allies, but ends if attention is drawn to the group. Darklings don't have the power end if noticed (so if a guard spots the motley and they incapacitate the guard, the Contract reasserts itself), and Ogres can use Stamina instead of Dexterity for how many allies they can help. Court Contracts follow a similar model but don't have the Seeming bonus, and there's still the Mantle/Goodwill considerations. Goblin Contracts now have a Goblin Debt system rather than each Contract having a unique negative quirk to it.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd quirks are mostly the same, but start a bit lower so the low level stuff is more likely to come into play for average games.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-05T16:38:26-07:00","id":1480218,"title":"","content":"One big thing is that personal frailties have changed from occupying the top half of the Wyrd ladder to coming in at every other dot; you still won't have a major frailty until the point you can have superhuman Trait ratings, but any changeling with a Wyrd over 1 has something magically messing with their ability to interact with the world in a wholly normal fashion aside from iron.<br /> <br /> Entitlements also now share part of their mechanical niche with kiths, in that both provide means of getting exceptional success more easily on a given Skill, which gels well with Hedgespinning and oneiromancy now having a system that relies on exceptional successes for its higher-level effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T13:53:26-07:00","id":1480308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480214#post1480214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to assume you mean from 1e to 2e?<br /> <br /> The Seasonal Courts didn't change much practically. There is a new mechanic for when a Court in ascendant that controls the Gentry to help make the Court's protective nature more clear. While they don't stop the Fae completely, they do force and conflicts into specific and predictable patterns that help give the Lost an edge. The metaphysical underpinnings of the Courts is more defined, allowing (in theory, but we don't have Court Contract creation rules) easier construction of alternative Court systems or coexisting Court systems.<br /> <br /> Entitlements have been reworked rather thoroughly. Their mechanics are better defined in general, but the big change is that they're usually more personal now. Entitlements are now unique titles only one being can have at a time. There can be Legion Entitlements, where the stories of multiple Entitlements are closely interconnected allowing for things closer to 1e's organized groups, but while they share an overarching theme, each member has a unique place. There could be The Knights of the Round Table with multiple members, but there can only be one King, one Lancelot, etc.<br /> <br /> Contracts were changed significantly as well. Arcadian Contracts (replacing Universal and Seeming ones) are sorted into six Regalia themes (each Seeming favors one), and withing each Regalia there are common and royal Contracts. Royal are treated as better, mildly, and are more big and flashy than practical and subtle. There are no longer 1-5 ratings in them, each one is a separate power of its own. Arcadian Contracts also have additional bonuses that you get for free if they match your Seeming, but can be learned at cost by anyone. For example Cloak of Night gives a stealth boost to you and Dexterity allies, but ends if attention is drawn to the group. Darklings don't have the power end if noticed (so if a guard spots the motley and they incapacitate the guard, the Contract reasserts itself), and Ogres can use Stamina instead of Dexterity for how many allies they can help. Court Contracts follow a similar model but don't have the Seeming bonus, and there's still the Mantle/Goodwill considerations. Goblin Contracts now have a Goblin Debt system rather than each Contract having a unique negative quirk to it.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd quirks are mostly the same, but start a bit lower so the low level stuff is more likely to come into play for average games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes I wanted to know what the changes were made from the first edition to the second edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T16:39:52-07:00","id":1480322,"title":"","content":"Another change is with the life extension raising the wyrd gives you. In 1e, your life span increased wyrd x10 years. In 2e, you just get 20+ years for each level of wyrd, though I am hoping you get a bigger boost upon reaching wyrd 7, though we might have to wait until the epic rule book to find out. I am hoping that they will give you ideas on how to make a changeling immortal so you can introduce characters like Alice Liddell, Hansel and Gretel, Morgana Le Fay, Vasilisa the Pure, and Korshei the Deathless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T21:05:37-07:00","id":1480332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480322#post1480322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another change is with the life extension raising the wyrd gives you. In 1e, your life span increased wyrd x10 years. In 2e, you just get 20+ years for each level of wyrd, though I am hoping you get a bigger boost upon reaching wyrd 7, though we might have to wait until the epic rule book to find out. I am hoping that they will give you ideas on how to make a changeling immortal so you can introduce characters like Alice Liddell, Hansel and Gretel, Morgana Le Fay, Vasilisa the Pure, and Korshei the Deathless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Companion supplement <b>Oak, Ash and Thorns</b> gives us <i>the Empty</i>, changeling's who cut out their heart and replaced it with a Token. One of the benefits of Emptying yourself is immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T21:16:49-07:00","id":1480334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480332#post1480332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Companion supplement <b>Oak, Ash and Thorns</b> gives us <i>the Empty</i>, changeling's who cut out their heart and replaced it with a Token. One of the benefits of Emptying yourself is immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I really want to explore how the wyrd makes the changeling evolve and potentially become something greater. I don't think reaching wyrd 10 should be the only way to gain immortality, but I WOULD like to see how a high wyrd and being a famous fairytale might transform some of our favorite folklore characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T21:24:31-07:00","id":1480336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480334#post1480334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I really want to explore how the wyrd makes the changeling evolve and potentially become something greater. I don't think reaching wyrd 10 should be the only way to gain immortality, but I WOULD like to see how a high wyrd and being a famous fairytale might transform some of our favorite folklore characters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Dunno about high Wyrd, but Entitlements (as others described above) seem to be the default official option for now for things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-06T23:23:21-07:00","id":1480347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480336#post1480336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Dunno about high Wyrd, but Entitlements (as others described above) seem to be the default official option for now for things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am hoping that having the seeming and kith evolve will carry over from 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T09:08:15-07:00","id":1480366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480332#post1480332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Companion supplement <b>Oak, Ash and Thorns</b> gives us <i>the Empty</i>, changeling's who cut out their heart and replaced it with a Token. One of the benefits of Emptying yourself is immortality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm glad that Changelings have an even longer lifespan now and I will have to find the second edition of Changeling The Lost and see how my favorite Seeming &amp; Kiths were changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 05-07-2022, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:57:47-07:00","id":1480403,"title":"","content":"Kiths were largely absent in the core (they have <i>twelve</i>) and relegated to a supplement that still hasn't come out. One day, perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T13:58:46-07:00","id":1480404,"title":"","content":"Well... fair warning since you didn't ask about those two:<br /> <br /> The broad strokes of Seemings are pretty much the same, though you might find characters from 1e might fit different Seemings better now due to some adjustments in focus; they're a lot more mentality focused with Kiths taking up more of the physical focus of how a changeling was shaped by their Durance. A 1e Beast of mine is one I'd do as an Ogre in 2e based on the new versions for example, because while he was changed into an animal shape his Durance forced him into a life of Brutality that drove him to become very mindful of the violence he was capable of and how to use it properly. Each Seeming grants you one bonus Attribute dot to a horizontal category (Power/Finesse/Resistance) Attribute of your choice, grants you a favored Regalia (you get to pick a second) rather than Contracts saying they're favored by a given Seeming, Blessings have been reworked to be more consistent, and the Curse are all Clarity damage sources (basically the CtL 2e version of breaking points) rather than mechanical drawbacks to certain actions.<br /> <br /> The real big change is that Kiths are no longer linked to Seemings. You can combine any Seeming with any Kith. This cuts down a lot on the need for multiple overlapping Kiths (like how many water-themed ones there are) so each Seeming has one, and we're probably not going to see Dual Kith come back since it's no longer needed to get a Kith from a different Seeming's list. Kith's are a lot more even in power, with a more standardized model (a Skill where you get an Exceptional Success on 3 successes instead of 5 when applying it to the Kith's themes on top of the more familiar Blessings, but the new Blessings tend to be a bit meatier).<br /> <br /> However, be prepared because the current Kith list is... short. Part of the design is to make it shorter in general, but the official ones printed so far don't cover a lot of things that were covered by the end of 1e.<br /> <br /> Edit: Yes, 12 feels tiny compared to the 1e core, but remember that with the decoupling, that's 72 possible combinations in 2e core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 05-07-2022, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T14:16:52-07:00","id":1480411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480366#post1480366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm glad that Changelings have an even longer lifespan now and I will have to find the second edition of Changeling The Lost and see how my favorite Seeming &amp; Kiths were changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind though, the Empty 1) are not in the 2e corebook, and 2) had to make some tradeoffs for the cost of their immortality \u2014 but then again, fairy magic in this game tends to be like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-07T19:42:26-07:00","id":1480441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1480206-what-changes-have-been-made-to-changeling-the-lost?p=1480411#post1480411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Keep in mind though, the Empty 1) are not in the 2e corebook, and 2) had to make some tradeoffs for the cost of their immortalit